{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on comparing the variances of the two lotteries and preferring the one with the larger variance. To compute variance, we need the squared deviations from the expected value, weighted by their probabilities. Both lotteries have an expected value of -6 Euros: Lottery A: (-6000) * 0.001 + 0 * 0.999 = -6; Lottery B: (-3000) * 0.002 + 0 * 0.998 = -6. Variance of A: ( (-6000 - (-6))^2 ) * 0.001 + ( (0 - (-6))^2 ) * 0.999 ≈ (5994^2)*0.001 + (6^2)*0.999 ≈ 35,928,036 * 0.001 + 36 * 0.999 ≈ 35,928.036 + 35.964 ≈ 35,964. Variance of B: ( (-3000 - (-6))^2 ) * 0.002 + ( (0 - (-6))^2 ) * 0.998 ≈ (2994^2)*0.002 + (6^2)*0.998 ≈ 8,964,036 * 0.002 + 36 * 0.998 ≈ 17,928.072 + 35.928 ≈ 17,964. Thus, variance of A (~35,964) is larger than variance of B (~17,964). The reason would prefer Lottery A. The decision reason is applicable to this problem.",
